## Agent Session Management

The orchestrator tracks the `session_handle` returned by every spawned agent. On loop-back, always prefer resuming over spawning:

| Situation | Action |
|---|---|
| Loop-back to a stage whose agent is still active | **Resume** — the selected adapter's resume operation to the saved `session_handle` with the new feedback |
| Loop-back but session has expired or ID is unavailable | **Spawn** — the selected adapter's spawn operation with a fully self-contained prompt |
| First entry to any stage | **Spawn** — the selected adapter's spawn operation |

Resuming keeps the agent's full prior context so it can act on feedback immediately without re-reading everything from scratch.

**Session ID update rule:** Only overwrite a saved session ID when a **new agent is spawned**. When resuming via the selected adapter's resume operation, do not change the stored ID — the interaction does not produce a new session.

